      "subject": "feat(missions): missions complete only on evidence (MS-4, ADR-0044)",
      "body": "Implements ADR-0044 Decision 5. Five checks: every task done or dropped by the owner with a reason; the latest linked commit verified by the owner as passing npm run build (a new commit needs its own verification); no linked approval pending; the plan's required documents committed at HEAD; a recovery anchor recorded. Runtime, as the system, moves an executing mission to validating once no task is left and completes it only when every check passes; a failed check keeps it validating. Task status and build verifications are owner-only, enforced at the Runtime boundary too, so the Chief Agent never validates or completes. Missions in execution are re-evaluated after every learning cycle. Runtime suites 1569/1569.\n\nMission: MS-2026-0001\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AHtXdN7VRusNxTFHzk5uFe",
